/ Signed in but unverified means they cannot post at all. That was previously
/ one muted line at the foot of the forum list, with no way to get the email
/ resent — most people who hit it simply never posted.
- return unless logged_in? && !current_user.email_verified?
- return if controller_path.in?(%w[sessions registrations passwords email_verifications email_changes])

.alert.alert-warning.d-flex.align-items-center.justify-content-between.flex-wrap.gap-2.mb-3 role="alert"
  div
    strong One more step:
    |  confirm your email address to post in the forum.
    br
    span.small
      | We sent a link to
      strong<>  = current_user.email_address
      | . Check your spam folder if it isn't there.
  = button_to "Resend the email", resend_email_verification_path, method: :post, class: "btn btn-warning btn-sm", form: { style: "display:inline;" }
